<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henry Parkes</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1815">1815</a>–<a href="/years/1896">1896</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Sir Henry Parkes</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henry Parkes was an English-born journalist and politician who served five times as premier of New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-wales">South Wales</a> between 1872 and 1891. He promoted free public education and free trade. His <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenterfield-oration">Tenterfield Oration</a> of 1889 launched the federation movement, earning him the name Father of Federation, although he died before the Commonwealth of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a> was created in 1901.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/henry-parkes.jpg" alt="Henry Parkes" width="320" height="419" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Henryparkes.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>From the 1880s concern about French and German colonies in the Pacific, Asian immigration and intercolonial trade encouraged the movement for federation, famously advanced by <b>Henry Parkes</b>, premier of New South Wales, in his Tenterfield Oration of 1889.</blockquote><a href="/empire/commonwealth-of-australia">Commonwealth of Australia · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>Under premiers such as <b>Henry Parkes</b>, a leading advocate of federation, New South Wales joined the other colonies to form the Commonwealth of Australia on 1 January 1901, becoming a state.</blockquote><a href="/state/colony-of-new-south-wales">Colony of New South Wales</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warwickshire">Warwickshire</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/united-kingdom">the United Kingdom</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sydney">Sydney</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/australia">Australia</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=52.33,-1.58&amp;year=1867" aria-label="Warwickshire on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4514 357 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Henry Parkes"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4964 627h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4964 627h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=52.33,-1.58&amp;year=1867">What was here in 1867? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
